sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Confidence-based early-exit inference
  accDescr: After training, a single AG News sample runs through Transformer layers. Classifier heads at layers two, four, and six produce confidence scores. Inference returns when confidence reaches the chosen threshold or the last head is reached.
  autonumber
  participant Eval as Evaluator
  participant Token as Tokenizer
  participant Model as Transformer
  participant Heads as Exit heads
  participant Metrics

  Note over Eval,Heads: Inference uses the jointly trained checkpoint
  Eval->>Token: Tokenize one test sample
  Token-->>Eval: Token IDs and attention mask
  Eval->>Model: Predict with threshold tau
  Model->>Model: Add token and position embeddings
  loop Remaining layers, until a prediction returns
    Model->>Model: Compute next Transformer block
    opt Head after layer 2, 4, or 6
      Model->>Heads: Pool unmasked hidden states
      Heads-->>Model: Class logits and max softmax confidence
      alt Confidence meets tau or final layer reached
        break Return prediction
          Model-->>Eval: Logits, exit layer, and confidence
        end
      else Below tau before the final layer
        Model->>Model: Continue to the next layer
      end
    end
  end
  Eval->>Metrics: Record accuracy, elapsed time, and power estimate
